{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00283",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 4.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.43,
      "end_seconds": 9.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.06,
      "end_seconds": 18.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Mainly I've been losing weight without trying. That's why I came. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.31,
      "end_seconds": 21.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.09,
      "end_seconds": 28.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "It's been like this since last Tuesday. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.28,
      "end_seconds": 31.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Mm. What about a cough, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.63,
      "end_seconds": 35.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.59,
      "end_seconds": 39.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.88,
      "end_seconds": 50.87,
      "duration_seconds": 10.99,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say. As for night sweats, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.29,
      "end_seconds": 65.63,
      "duration_seconds": 13.34,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.29,
      "end_seconds": 67.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.44,
      "end_seconds": 71.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Right, any blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.89,
      "end_seconds": 75.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "No, you know, no blood in the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.58,
      "end_seconds": 83.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Alright, have you had any diarrhoea, lumps in the neck, shortness of breath or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.86,
      "end_seconds": 85.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.19,
      "end_seconds": 92.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.76,
      "end_seconds": 106.25,
      "duration_seconds": 12.49,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 107.12,
      "end_seconds": 115.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Blood pressure 124 over 75, respiratory rate 22. Temperature is 38.4 degrees, pulse 97, saturation 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.34,
      "end_seconds": 117.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.32,
      "end_seconds": 121.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just typing this up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.29,
      "end_seconds": 132.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Good, where were we. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.21,
      "end_seconds": 142.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "Just my appendix out, about eight years ago. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.91,
      "end_seconds": 147.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.02,
      "end_seconds": 148.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.54,
      "end_seconds": 169.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.09,
      "end_seconds": 172.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "No, um, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.0,
      "end_seconds": 176.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.36,
      "end_seconds": 178.17,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.54,
      "end_seconds": 194.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.69,
      "end_seconds": 206.83,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "Metformin. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar. I mean, you know, it's Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.8,
      "end_seconds": 219.85,
      "duration_seconds": 12.05,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.0,
      "end_seconds": 222.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.41,
      "end_seconds": 225.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.52,
      "end_seconds": 228.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.22,
      "end_seconds": 234.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.04,
      "end_seconds": 238.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.52,
      "end_seconds": 244.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.7,
      "end_seconds": 247.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.24,
      "end_seconds": 253.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.39,
      "end_seconds": 264.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.83,
      "text": "I have diabetes. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I have COPD, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.72,
      "end_seconds": 268.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Okay. Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.57,
      "end_seconds": 272.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Well, it's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.48,
      "end_seconds": 275.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.01,
      "end_seconds": 277.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.62,
      "end_seconds": 280.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Alright, breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.35,
      "end_seconds": 294.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Air entry is a bit reduced at the top of the right lung."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.3,
      "end_seconds": 322.56,
      "duration_seconds": 23.26,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.7,
      "end_seconds": 327.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.98,
      "end_seconds": 337.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with an infection or something chronic going on, I can't say what yet. I'd also keep tuberculosis in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.66,
      "end_seconds": 341.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Okay, so is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.78,
      "end_seconds": 359.25,
      "duration_seconds": 17.47,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an infection or something chronic going on, I can't say what yet, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been losing weight without trying, since last Tuesday, and no shortness of breath or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.71,
      "end_seconds": 362.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.91,
      "end_seconds": 378.83,
      "duration_seconds": 15.92,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.88,
      "end_seconds": 381.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.91,
      "end_seconds": 405.54,
      "duration_seconds": 22.63,
      "text": "Let's get a sputum test, for chronic cough. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's get a chest X-ray, for weight loss and cough. Weigh yourself once a week at the same time and note it down. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.4,
      "end_seconds": 413.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if you cough up blood or get breathless. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.69,
      "end_seconds": 415.39,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.52,
      "end_seconds": 424.91,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a week. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 426.51,
      "end_seconds": 430.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "So, I come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.7,
      "end_seconds": 437.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.7,
      "end_seconds": 442.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "No, you know, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.69,
      "end_seconds": 443.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}